Z||000010||AusFiero||06-15-2001||07:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by CoolBlue87GT:<BR><B>NICE !!  What software are you using to do this.   It's wild!   I want it !!!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Good old reliable Adobe Photoshop CoolBlue. I have version 6.<P>To change colurs copy the area manually and save it as a new layer. Use Hue & Saturation to change the colours and balance out the brightness and contrast to bring them back to reality. If you can't get quite the shade you are after use colour balance to adjust them.<P>Thats pretty much all there is to it. See this thread <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/002327.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/002327.html</A>  for more recoloured cars. Porsche Carreras in this case. Yes it is in the off topic area.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
